# Development Workflow

Every feature or change follows this order — **do not skip steps**.

## 1. Plan in docs first

Before writing code, add or update a plan under `docs/plans/`:

- File name: `docs/plans/<feature-name>.md` (e.g. `quote-endpoint.md`)
- Include: goal, scope, API/schema changes, test cases, files to touch
- Get the plan written and reviewed before implementation starts

No implementation until the plan document exists.

## 2. Implement with tests

Every implementation **must** include tests in the same change:

- New function, endpoint, or service → add unit and/or integration tests
- Bug fix → add a regression test that fails without the fix
- Do not merge or consider work done without passing tests

Run `pytest` before marking the task complete.

## 3. Update documentation after implementation

When implementation is done, update docs to match the code:

- `README.md` — setup, commands, env vars, behavior changes
- `docs/SPEC.md` or plan file — mark plan as done, note any deviations
- `.env.example` — new or changed environment variables
- Inline docstrings only where logic is non-obvious

Documentation updates are part of the same task, not a follow-up.

## Checklist (copy per task)

```
- [ ] Plan written in docs/plans/<feature>.md
- [ ] Code + tests implemented
- [ ] pytest passes
- [ ] README / docs / .env.example updated
```
